# Document face is Arial (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-10-08), verbatim:

> **Hard rule: do not use Calibri. Use Arial for your default.**

## The rule

> **Every rendered Word and PDF document uses Arial for body, headings,
> the cover company name, the header, and the footer. Do not use
> Calibri. Consolas is allowed only for code. Pin the document theme
> to Arial so Word cannot substitute Calibri or Cambria.**

## Required

| Surface | Face |
| --- | --- |
| Body, headings, quotes, tables, header, footer, cover name | **Arial** |
| Code blocks | Consolas |
| Theme (`ascii`, `hAnsi`, east Asia, complex script) | **Arial** |

`operator-workflows/scripts/docs/render-doc.py` and
`operator-workflows/scripts/contracts/render-contract.py` both name
Arial. `apply_brand_type` defaults to Arial.

## Forbidden

- Calibri on any run, style, or theme slot
- Inter, Urbanist, Aptos, or Segoe as a substitute default
- Calling a PDF done while its embedded faces still include Calibri

## Origin

2026-10-08 - operator hard rule after a Calibri render. Arial is the
default. Re-render every document that was set in Calibri.
